import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.Socket;

final class ManagedConnection implements AutoCloseable {
    private final Socket socket;

    ManagedConnection(Socket socket) {
        this.socket = socket;
    }

    @Override
    public void close() throws IOException {
        socket.close();
    }
}

class CleanupExample {
    static void send(Socket socket) throws IOException {
        try (var connection = new ManagedConnection(socket)) {
            // use connection
        } // close() runs on normal or exceptional exit from the try body
    }
}
```

The owner closes the resource at a known boundary. A finalizer cannot provide that timing guarantee.
